# action</make> creates a particle in its interface position<item>, and
# action</mid> moves it to position<box>. action</mid> also has a local
# position<item> whose constraint nothing uses, which is dead even though the
# particle in position<box> came from a callee's position<item>.
define the potential action<my.domain.com:my_lib:/test> {
    it also assigns the action</mid>.
    it happens when {
        this particle is created.
    } and it does {
        create a particle in action</mid>::position<run>.
        destroy the particle in action</mid>::position<box>.
    }
}
